# Constrained NVT with a Nose-Hoover thermostat.
#
# Nose-Hoover is used rather than Berendsen or velocity rescaling because it is
# the thermostat with a genuine extended-system formulation in this code base,
# and because its thermostat mass Q = dof * kB * T * tau^2 is computed from the
# AUTHORITATIVE constrained degree-of-freedom count. A run whose DOF silently
# reverted to the unconstrained 3N-3 would thermostat to the wrong kinetic
# energy, which is exactly what this case is here to catch.
#
# `velocity_init input` takes the velocities from the .xyz and `velocity_seed`
# is fixed, so the run is deterministic and reproducible. COM removal is ON, so
# the reported degree-of-freedom count is 3N - constraints - 3 = 36 - 12 - 3 = 21,
# which is clearly distinct from the unconstrained 3N - 3 = 33.
velocity 300.0        # also the thermostat target temperature [K]
time_step 0.5
run 400
output_interval 10
velocity_init input
velocity_seed 20260916
remove_com_velocity true
molecular_nonbonded special

thermostat nose_hoover
thermostat_tau 100.0

constraints on
constraint_tolerance 1e-10
constraint_max_iterations 500

write_checkpoint_every 400
checkpoint_file nvt_final.gmdchk
